WEBVTT

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:08.480
Collapse of the bearer confirmed.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:17.110
This Elemio Comb has divine powers. It nullifies all of your magic!

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:21.050
What the hell?

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:29.210
Burn him!

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:37.970
We need to run, Kuu. That's no Alpha Stigma!

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:22.730
Hey. Who are you?

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:26.920
God. Devil. Dark god. Hero. Monster.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:28.450
Call me what you will.

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:31.290
After all, you shall vanish.

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:40.300
That Sui man seemed surprised.

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:43.990
But the fact that you're not an ordinary Alpha Stigma bearer...

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:45.720
...isn't all that shocking.

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:50.470
After all, you were once a legendary perverted man of ill repute.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.530
And on top of being a sex fiend,

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:54.600
you're a lazy, good-for-nothing fop.

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:00.410
I've never told you this before,

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:04.320
but I read that report you wrote when Sion showed it to me.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:08.700
If I recall, there was a certain passage in it.

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:13.200
"People hate dying. They hate killing, too.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.430
They don't like making others cry, or crying themselves.

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:18.660
How must it feel not to be able to choose one's life?

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:22.340
What about when family dies? Or when a loved one dies?"

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:26.290
I thought that the person who wrote that must have been an idiot.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:28.550
People hate dying?

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:30.600
People die.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.440
They hate killing?

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:36.750
If someone lives, it means someone dies.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:39.930
As a lazy sloth who finds everything to be a pain,

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:42.100
and as the timid person that you are,

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:47.350
I highly doubt that you could ever possibly kill me.

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:48.660
That's what I think.

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:54.910
Hey, Ryner.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:58.700
You wanted to advance forward, didn't you?

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:01.690
You didn't like being called a monster, did you?

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:05.840
You thought to yourself that you were sick of killing people, didn't you?

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:10.350
I've already evaded your attacks five times now.

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:14.200
But I won't dodge the next. You can decide the rest.

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:22.900
I don't consider you a monster.

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:26.720
Got that? You're not a monster.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:30.910
You are my partner, my manservant, and my tea-drinking companion.

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:32.910
You're no monster.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.260
Can you hear me, Ryner?

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:43.990
Are you listening, Ryner?!

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:47.150
N-No...

00:04:48.170 --> 00:04:50.630
A-All of you...

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:53.100
Shut the fuck up.

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:56.930
You time is up now.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.590
Ryner!

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:13.700
Sorry, Ferris.

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:17.700
Close my eyes...

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:26.090
Ry... ner...

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:29.090
You're...

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:32.800
You're... not a monster.

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:36.100
You're not a monster!

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:59.590
I guess I really tried to kill you, huh?

00:05:59.590 --> 00:06:01.670
This is what I am.

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:04.240
Despised by everyone as taboo.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:06.730
A monster with no talents beyond killing.

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:11.850
But I don't want to kill people I know anymore.

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:15.370
So... You head back to Roland.

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:18.670
Sion wouldn't complain.

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:20.420
This journey is already over...

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:24.520
If you really intended to kill me, I would be dead right now.

00:06:25.130 --> 00:06:27.070
But I'm not dead.

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:32.280
A coward like you who can't kill a single woman calls himself a monster.

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:33.460
Don't make me laugh.

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:38.450
Now then, let's find a nice place somewhere and have some tea.

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:45.090
I still have some of the dumplings Iris brought for me.

00:06:56.740 --> 00:06:58.310
Welcome back.

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:02.850
Yeah.

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:07.520
I'm home.

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:19.070
<i>Two people of unknown origin, a man and a woman,</i>

00:07:19.070 --> 00:07:21.920
<i>used the hero relic, the Dolueli Swordscale,</i>

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:23.630
<i>and assaulted us.</i>

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:27.840
<i>They possessed two other hero relics,</i>

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:31.900
<i>and I believe that, like us, they are foreigners seeking to gather hero relics.</i>

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:35.010
<i>The outcome of the battle resulted in their escape.</i>

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:37.170
<i>Whether they survived or perished after that is unclear.</i>

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:41.700
Lord Astal!

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:45.000
How many more hours do you plan to keep working?

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:48.520
You still haven't even touched your meal!

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:50.320
Sorry, Eslina.

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:53.280
As soon as this is finished, I'll eat it all and rest a bit.

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:56.420
You're saying that again?

00:07:56.420 --> 00:08:00.450
Always with the morose expression. What is it this time?

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:03.470
I'm not so troubled that I need your sarcasm.

00:08:03.470 --> 00:08:07.310
And there you go, taking everything upon yourself again.

00:08:07.310 --> 00:08:09.010
I swear, you're such a...

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:12.660
At times like this, if you don't physically force Sion to stop,

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:15.370
he'll keep working until he collapses.

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:17.180
Remember that, okay, Eslina?

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:18.830
Right, Calne!

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:20.220
All of you...

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:22.740
If you push yourself too hard,

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:26.120
Fiole up in heaven will get so worried he'll have to come back down here!

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:27.670
Right, Eslina?

00:08:27.670 --> 00:08:30.200
Right! You mustn't do that, your Majesty.

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:33.810
Please don't do anything that would make my brother sad!

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:37.060
To be blessed with subordinates so concerned for their lord,

00:08:37.060 --> 00:08:39.770
the King of Roland must be quite happy.

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:41.690
Ah, Lady Noa Ehn.

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:44.720
Have you grown accustomed to life in Roland?

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:47.410
Yes. With your Majesty's kind consideration,

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:49.980
I have had quite a pleasant stay.

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:52.930
Rear Admiral Klom also treats me quite well.

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:55.340
Oh? Claugh, hm?

00:08:55.710 --> 00:09:01.060
Looks like we were dead on having Sir Claugh act as Lady Noa's guide.

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:02.350
So it would seem.

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:05.100
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:06.940
Did you have some business with Sion?

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:10.250
Business? Have you forgotten?

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:12.940
We had dinner arrangements for tonight.

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:17.600
Oh? I thought you said you had a dinner party tonight?

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:21.870
No, that's tomorrow. Er, it was postponed to tomorrow.

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:24.060
Oh, is that right?

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:27.140
S-Sorry. I got busy, and things came up...

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:28.610
I understand.

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:32.990
I know that you stay busy with "things", Rear Admiral.

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:36.310
Calne, I hope you're not telling Noa anything unnecessary...

00:09:36.310 --> 00:09:38.310
What would something unnecessary be?

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:40.290
E-Erm that is...

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:46.050
I'd like to hear all about it at greater length over dinner.

00:09:46.050 --> 00:09:49.390
On that note, your Majesty, I shall be borrowing your Rear Admiral for a bit.

00:09:49.390 --> 00:09:51.140
By all means, by all means.

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:53.280
W-Well, er...

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:02.710
Sir Claugh and Lady Noa, hm?

00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:07.680
Lady Noa has become something of a hostage for Estabul's sake.

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:09.550
I hope that having Claugh remain at her side

00:10:09.550 --> 00:10:11.860
will give her at least a little bit of support.

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:14.530
I'm sure she'll be fine.

00:10:21.790 --> 00:10:25.600
Have you taken a moment to glance over my written opinion?

00:10:25.820 --> 00:10:29.100
Yes. The state of affairs in the northern region

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:31.600
seems to have finally grown dire.

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:36.610
Imperial Stohl boasts strong forces in the northern region.

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:41.070
There, at the present time, are invasions advancing at a breakneck speed,

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:44.630
led by the emergent royal family of Gastark, in the northernmost region of the continent.

00:10:44.630 --> 00:10:48.920
Gastark has been annexing neighboring small kingdoms, one after another.

00:10:48.920 --> 00:10:51.860
The equilibrium of the Menoris Continent has begun to collapse.

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:55.030
I believe that eventually, the onset of war will be inevitable.

00:10:57.530 --> 00:11:01.840
Our most pressing business is an urgently needed unification of the Roland Empire.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:04.090
If we don't make a clean sweep of the nobles' power

00:11:04.090 --> 00:11:06.770
and bring the kingdom together internally,

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:09.810
this country will be engulfed in the ravaging vortex of war, and will dissapear.

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:13.000
For that reason, what you must do now is...

00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:16.130
A political purge, is it?

00:11:16.130 --> 00:11:20.700
That would be the quickest way to stabilize the Roland Empire.

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:22.990
But, that would be...

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:27.290
You are indeed a superior, excellent king.

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:30.290
If you were to take your time as you are and keep changing this kingdom,

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:34.070
someday all of the people of the land would follow you, I'm sure.

00:11:34.070 --> 00:11:40.590
But by that time, would Roland already be destroyed by another kingdom?

00:11:40.990 --> 00:11:45.720
Regardless of your decision, I shall simply follow your will.

00:11:53.690 --> 00:11:57.310
I'm always hearing of your accomplishments.

00:11:57.310 --> 00:12:01.110
I was thinking it might be nice to speak with you at length, for once.

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:05.070
After all, you're not like all the youngsters elevated in status thanks to the young king.

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:07.990
You're someone closer to our status.

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:12.830
I too, have desired to talk with you, Duke.

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:14.940
Is that right?

00:12:14.940 --> 00:12:19.120
Do you feel anything, working beneath that young king?

00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:24.170
Let's see. Disappointingly, my opinions never seem to quite reach him.

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:25.880
He's certainly soft.

00:12:25.880 --> 00:12:28.050
The fact that he doesn't prioritize taking advantages in his actions

00:12:28.050 --> 00:12:30.220
makes things awkward for me, to be honest.

00:12:30.490 --> 00:12:32.080
I thought as much.

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:33.810
Then, you understand, don't you?

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:38.110
You can tell which side would be more advantageous to join.

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:42.340
There are scant few sharp men such as yourself among the nobles.

00:12:42.340 --> 00:12:45.440
I could make you my right-hand man.

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:48.740
You could have any reward you wished.

00:12:49.710 --> 00:12:55.620
You, much like the other nobles, are rather slow-witted, aren't you?

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:57.000
Wha—?

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:59.400
Any reward I wish?

00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:01.320
It would be impossible for you.

00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:05.330
It is something that only Lord Sion Astal can make a reality.

00:13:05.330 --> 00:13:09.890
Only Lord Astal, a true ruler who allows the weak and the strong to coexist.

00:13:10.570 --> 00:13:13.980
My revered king is far too kind.

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:17.960
He even seeks to save the worms that crawl right before his eyes.

00:13:17.960 --> 00:13:20.750
That is why I must act in his stead,

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:23.900
to crush each and every one of them.

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:26.780
Let me ask you, instead.

00:13:28.430 --> 00:13:30.630
With whom will you side?

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:37.220
The old forces that dwell within this nation,

00:13:37.220 --> 00:13:39.180
or my king?

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:49.970
over my standing you up with our dinner arrangements.

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:53.390
Not at all. Do I look like the kind of woman

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:56.130
who would constantly get upset over such petty matters?

00:13:56.130 --> 00:14:00.140
No, but... Well, women are complicated, y'know.

00:14:00.140 --> 00:14:01.080
My.

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:05.370
You seem to be quite knowledgable about females, Rear Admiral Klom.

00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:10.180
I'm telling you, quit with the "Rear Admiral Klom" thing.

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:11.260
Claugh is fine.

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:15.160
I'm not really angry.

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:18.480
I simply haven't had many outings

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:20.360
where I remained out this late.

00:14:21.100 --> 00:14:24.490
And under such a pretty night sky...

00:14:25.330 --> 00:14:27.420
Is it that pretty?

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:31.210
Is it different looking up at the sky in Estabul?

00:14:31.210 --> 00:14:32.830
The sky is the same everywhere.

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:35.060
But, even looking at the same sky,

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:39.060
the feeling you get from seeing it changes depending on who you're with, right?

00:14:40.470 --> 00:14:41.980
Is that how it works?

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:47.700
I am truly glad that Roland has a person like yourself.

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:50.090
Nothing.

00:14:50.090 --> 00:14:52.550
Today was truly fun.

00:14:52.550 --> 00:14:54.030
Thank you, Claugh.

00:14:57.940 --> 00:14:59.790
Sorry for staying out this late.

00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:11.860
You're a smart lady.

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:15.010
You seem to understand the position you've been placed in.

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:19.550
If I scream, you'll kill everyone. Is that it?

00:15:19.550 --> 00:15:23.000
Then, I'd like for you to comply with my orders.

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:25.190
First, shall we have those clothes come off?

00:15:33.650 --> 00:15:37.240
Geez, I just don't get women.

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:44.910
Claugh!

00:15:45.950 --> 00:15:46.500
Stop!

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:53.130
Damn it!

00:15:57.020 --> 00:15:58.390
Noa! Are you all right?!

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:25.040
What have you done to her?

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:26.460
Nothing, yet.

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:27.550
Nothing?

00:16:27.550 --> 00:16:29.890
Then why is she crying?

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:32.340
In any event, you can't do anything.

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:34.010
Not with that wound.

00:16:34.010 --> 00:16:36.490
That's not what I asked.

00:16:36.490 --> 00:16:38.990
Why is Noa crying?!

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:40.650
That's what I asked!

00:16:40.650 --> 00:16:42.100
What I seek is thunder!

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:52.570
We should be able to see and smell our goal, the town of Regit, very soon.

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:56.900
Rumor has it that the town of Regit is cursed by a devil.

00:16:58.130 --> 00:17:02.560
It might offer us a solid lead on a hero relic. Right, Ryner?

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:10.240
Let's get moving.

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:12.150
Huh?

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:17.680
Ryner, right now we've been charged with an important mission.

00:17:18.290 --> 00:17:20.820
A mission to protect the freedom of all dumplings

00:17:20.820 --> 00:17:23.580
from the grip of that overbearing king!

00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:25.430
What the hell are you talking about?

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:29.840
I shall do my utmost for the dumplings' sake.

00:17:41.070 --> 00:17:43.130
Hey, wait up!

00:17:45.300 --> 00:17:47.100
Hold it right there, brat!

00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:48.860
Don't do anything stupid!

00:17:48.860 --> 00:17:50.400
You won't get away, you little...!

00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:52.840
No! Let go! Please!

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:54.720
Knock it off!

00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:58.370
Do you have any idea what trouble you all have caused for us—

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:03.760
Bro, it's not very cool to beat up children, you know.

00:18:03.760 --> 00:18:05.390
What's your problem, you—

00:18:12.280 --> 00:18:13.610
Hey. You okay?

00:18:14.100 --> 00:18:16.650
Help me! Please, help me!

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:17.760
Calm down.

00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:19.570
Arua... Save Arua!

00:18:19.980 --> 00:18:23.000
Please, she's just different! Arua's just different!

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:23.740
Arua?

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:26.850
Arua is not a monster!

00:18:29.190 --> 00:18:34.280
Please, save Arua! Arua's no monster!

00:18:39.490 --> 00:18:43.810
Thanks to the efforts of Rear Admiral Klom who by good fortune happened to be nearby,

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:45.510
it ended without incident.

00:18:46.090 --> 00:18:49.680
Roland and Estabul are following a path of reconciliation,

00:18:49.680 --> 00:18:52.070
based upon Lady Noa's existence.

00:18:52.070 --> 00:18:57.650
If she had died just then, another revolt would have become inevitable.

00:18:57.650 --> 00:19:02.650
And their anger would naturally be focused upon your Majesty, as Lady Noa's protector.

00:19:03.720 --> 00:19:05.820
It's just like them.

00:19:05.820 --> 00:19:08.420
They don't consider what benefits the country at all.

00:19:08.420 --> 00:19:11.730
They'll stop at nothing to take me down,

00:19:11.730 --> 00:19:13.750
to get all the influence they want.

00:19:14.080 --> 00:19:17.750
What choice will your Majesty make moving forward?

00:19:18.280 --> 00:19:19.760
The path you've shown me?

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:22.500
It is as I told you before.

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:24.490
First, ingratiate yourself with the nobility.

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:28.810
Even if they sought Lady Noa's life, your Majesty must not press them.

00:19:28.810 --> 00:19:32.380
Accept them, and feed them sweet honey.

00:19:32.380 --> 00:19:34.520
Get them to lower their guard.

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:34.530
And then...
Get them to lower their guard.

00:19:34.530 --> 00:19:35.690
And then...

00:19:35.690 --> 00:19:37.280
Slaughter them all?

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:38.980
If necessary.

00:19:38.980 --> 00:19:40.470
But what of the people?

00:19:40.470 --> 00:19:44.200
In that short amount of time, many people will be oppressed,

00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:45.920
and many more will die of starvation.

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:48.280
What of it?

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:52.100
I have everything prepared already.

00:19:52.100 --> 00:19:54.650
All I need is your order.

00:19:55.730 --> 00:19:58.420
It wasn't you that had Lady Noa attacked, was it?

00:19:59.640 --> 00:20:02.870
It is a rather exciting tactic, isn't it?

00:20:02.870 --> 00:20:07.270
However, I unfortunately had no hand in this matter.

00:20:07.990 --> 00:20:09.300
You may leave.

00:20:09.300 --> 00:20:10.130
Sir.

00:20:26.670 --> 00:20:29.620
Arua is my childhood friend.

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:32.040
We all got along well and lived together.

00:20:32.450 --> 00:20:36.460
Our lord suddenly raised the village's taxes extremely high.

00:20:36.720 --> 00:20:39.260
Then a bunch of his soldiers came to the village.

00:20:39.260 --> 00:20:43.470
My mother and my father were both killed.

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:47.060
The soldiers tried to kill me, too.

00:20:47.060 --> 00:20:50.910
When they did, Arua suddenly... used magic...

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:53.080
Arua!

00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:56.870
Arua had never used magic before.

00:20:56.870 --> 00:20:59.630
And, in Arua's eyes...

00:21:00.790 --> 00:21:03.110
Everyone's calling Arua a monster!

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:07.600
The lord and soldiers took her away, saying they'd investigate in detail!

00:21:07.600 --> 00:21:11.340
Please! Arua... Save Arua!

00:21:12.010 --> 00:21:13.160
All right.

00:21:13.420 --> 00:21:15.020
Shall we be off?

00:21:16.210 --> 00:21:19.500
We can't leave an Alpha Stigma to chance.

00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:21.890
It could run wild at any time.

00:21:21.890 --> 00:21:23.160
That's...

00:21:23.160 --> 00:21:26.660
Or do you have another problem with this?

00:21:30.910 --> 00:21:33.990
Do you know where Arua was taken?

00:21:33.990 --> 00:21:36.660
Ah, it was probably...

00:21:41.440 --> 00:21:43.590
I see. Over there, hm?

00:23:20.410 --> 00:23:24.580
<i>Alpha Stigma? Devil's eyes?</i>

00:23:24.580 --> 00:23:26.540
<i>Bah, this sucks!</i>

00:23:26.540 --> 00:23:29.840
<i>All of you, quit dragging me into this crap!</i>

00:23:29.840 --> 00:23:33.170
<i>I don't have these eyes because I like them, you know!</i>

00:23:33.170 --> 00:23:34.220
<i>This sucks.</i>
